[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Exploring the Sea-Floor]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.93]Lesson 30 | 第30课
[00:02.38]Exploring the sea-floor | 海底勘探
[00:09.48]How did people probably imagine the sea-floor before it was investigated? | 在海底得到考察之前，人们可能怎样想像它？
[00:17.45]Our knowledge of the oceans a hundred years ago was confined to the two-dimensional shape of the sea surface | 一百年前，我们对海洋的了解仅限于海面的二维形状，
[00:24.90]and the hazards of navigation presented by the irregularities in depth of the shallow water close to the land. | 以及近陆浅水区深度的不规则给航海带来的危险。
[00:33.53]The open sea was deep and mysterious, | 远海深邃而神秘，
[00:36.86]and anyone who gave more than a passing thought to the bottom confines of the oceans probably assumed that the sea-bed was flat. | 任何对海底深处稍稍想过一想的人多半会认为海底是平坦的。
[00:45.67]Sir James Clark Ross had obtained a sounding of over 2, 400 fathoms in 1839, | 詹姆斯·克拉克·罗斯爵士早在1839年就测得2400多英寻的深度，
[00:53.26]but it was not until 1869, when H.M.S. Porcupine was put at the disposal of the Royal Society for several cruises | 但直到1869年，皇家海军“豪猪”号被拨给皇家学会进行几次巡航考察时，
[01:03.38]that a series of deep soundings was obtained in the Atlantic and the first samples were collected by dredging the bottom. | 才在大西洋测得一系列深水测深数据，并通过疏浚海底采集了第一批样品。
[01:11.84]Shortly after this the famous H.M.S. Challenger expedition established the study of the sea-floor | 此后不久，著名的皇家海军“挑战者”号探险确立了海底研究的地位，
[01:19.01]as a subject worthy of the most qualified physicists and geologists. | 使之成为值得最有资历的物理学家和地质学家研究的课题。
[01:24.37]A burst of activity associated with the laying of submarine cables | 铺设海底电缆带来的一阵热潮
[01:29.62]soon confirmed the Challenger's observation that many parts of the ocean were two to three miles deep, | 很快证实了“挑战者”号的观察结果：海洋的许多地方深达两到三英里，
[01:37.28]and the existence of underwater features of considerable magnitude. | 还证实了规模相当大的水下地貌的存在。
[01:42.74]Today, enough soundings are available to enable a relief map of the Atlantic to be drawn | 今天，已有足够的测深数据可以绘制一张大西洋的立体地图，
[01:49.02]and we know something of the great variety of the sea bed's topography. | 我们对海底地形的千姿百态也已有所了解。
[01:54.78]Since the sea covers the greater part of the earth's surface, | 既然海洋覆盖了地球表面的大部分，
[01:58.56]it is quite reasonable to regard the sea floor as the basic form of the crust of the earth, | 把海底看作地壳的基本形态是非常合理的，
[02:04.88]with superimposed upon it the continents, | 大陆叠加在它上面，
[02:08.74]together with the islands and other features of the oceans. | 还有岛屿和海洋的其他地貌。
[02:13.05]The continents form rugged tablelands which stand nearly three miles above the floor of the open ocean. | 大陆形成了崎岖不平的高地，高出开阔的洋底近三英里。
[02:20.95]From the shore line, out to a distance which may be anywhere from a few miles to a few hundred miles, | 从海岸线向外延伸可达几英里到几百英里的地方，
[02:28.63]runs the gentle slope of the continental shelf, geologically part of the continents. | 是大陆架的缓坡，在地质上属于大陆的一部分。
[02:35.45]The real dividing line between continents and oceans occurs at the foot of a steeper slope. | 大陆和海洋的真正分界线位于一道更陡的坡度的脚下。
[02:42.70]This continental slope usually starts at a place somewhere near the 100-fathom mark | 这道大陆坡通常始于100英寻线附近的某处，
[02:48.91]and in the course of a few hundred miles reaches the true ocean floor at 2, 500-3, 500 fathoms. | 在几百英里的行程内下降到2500～3500英寻的真正洋底。
[02:59.08]The slope averages about 1 in 30, but contains steep, | 坡度平均约为1比30，但包含陡峭的、
[03:03.49]probably vertical, cliffs, and gentle sediment-covered terraces, | 很可能是垂直的悬崖，以及覆盖着沉积物的平缓台阶，
[03:08.14]and near its lower reaches there is a long tailing-off which is almost certainly the result of | 在其下段有一条长长的缓倾尾端，它几乎肯定是
[03:14.36]material transported out to deep water after being eroded from the continental masses. | 从大陆块侵蚀下来后被搬运到深水中的物质的产物。
